                    ANALYTICS PROJECT CHECKLIST
         Keep this visible throughout your project - Check off as you go
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

WEEK 1: DISCOVER & DEFINE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

DAY 1: DISCOVERY
□ Research: Review existing reports, emails, documentation (45 min)
□ Prepare kickoff questions (business question, success criteria, scope)
□ Set up project folder structure (data, code, docs, deliverables)
□ Print this checklist and put on desk
□ Kickoff meeting: Ask critical questions, take detailed notes (60 min)
□ Draft project charter with business question, scope, deliverable format
□ Email charter to sponsor: "Does this match your expectations?"
⚠ RED FLAG: Writing code on Day 1? STOP. Do discovery first.

DAY 2: REQUIREMENTS
□ Create metrics dictionary (definition, formula, source, validation)
□ Map data sources and lineage (tables, joins, grain, latency)
□ Identify data quality concerns and document
□ Mock up final deliverable (PowerPoint sketch, dashboard layout, etc.)
□ Get stakeholder approval on mockup BEFORE building
□ Update charter with any changes from mockup review
⚠ RED FLAG: Vague metrics definitions? STOP. Get clarity in writing.

DAY 3: VALIDATION
□ Pull sample data from each source
□ Run data quality checks (completeness, accuracy, consistency)
□ Document data issues and resolution plan
□ Validate numbers against published reports
□ Create step-by-step analysis plan
□ Set up code structure and documentation
□ Schedule weekly check-ins (Monday mornings, 15-30 min)
⚠ RED FLAG: Numbers don't match reports? STOP. Figure out why first.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

WEEK 2-3: DEVELOP
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

EVERY MONDAY: CHECK-IN
□ Show work-in-progress (even if rough/incomplete)
□ Share what's working and what's blocked
□ Get feedback early and incorporate
□ Adjust timeline if needed
⚠ RED FLAG: Week 2 and sponsor hasn't seen anything? STOP. Show work today.

BUILD PHASE
□ Extract and prepare data (follow analysis plan)
□ Calculate metrics (reference metrics dictionary)
□ Validate calculations against known values
□ Create visualizations (match mockup format)
□ Document code as you write it
□ Keep changelog of major changes
□ Internal QA: Check for errors before showing
⚠ RED FLAG: Building complex logic and not sure why? STOP. Check charter.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

WEEK 4: DELIVER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

FINALIZE
□ Lead with the answer (executive summary / BLUF approach)
□ Tailor message to audience
□ Make insights actionable (So what? Now what?)
□ Professional formatting and polish
□ Final QA check (numbers, spelling, formatting)
□ Internal review before sending to stakeholder
⚠ RED FLAG: Just explaining what happened, not what to do? Add recommendations.

PRESENT
□ Present findings to stakeholder
□ Get feedback and next steps
□ Document action items and owners
□ Follow up on any open questions

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

WEEK 5: DOCUMENT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CLOSE OUT
□ Write lessons learned (what worked, what didn't, what to do next time)
□ Document code thoroughly (README, comments, logic)
□ Create runbook if recurring analysis
□ Knowledge transfer to team or stakeholders
□ Archive project files in organized structure
□ Update this framework with improvements

